---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, SELLER } from '../config';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of sale"
  description="Terms for buying and using AI Blog Writer Pro: licenses, the free trial, renewals and cancellation, the 14-day money-back guarantee, and your own AI and search accounts."
  schema={[breadcrumbNode([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Terms of sale', path: '/terms/' }])]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of sale</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated 14 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        These terms cover buying and using AI Blog Writer Pro ("Pro"), the paid add-on for {SITE.productName}. The free
        plugin is software you can use, change and share under its <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html">GPL
        license</a>, and this website is covered by the <a href="/privacy/">website privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who sells Pro</h2>
      <p>
        Freemius, Inc. sells Pro as our reseller and merchant of record: it runs the checkout, takes the payment, charges
        VAT where it applies, and issues your invoices.
        The <a href="https://freemius.com/terms/">Freemius terms</a> and <a href="https://freemius.com/privacy/">privacy policy</a> apply
        to the purchase and payment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pro is made by {SELLER.name}, {SELLER.description}{SELLER.address && `, ${SELLER.address}`}, who provides your
        license, updates and support under these terms. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Plans and licenses</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> lists the plans and prices, which exclude VAT. A Creator license runs Pro
        on 1 WordPress site at a time and an Agency license on up to 5. To move a license, deactivate it on one site and
        activate it on another.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pro's code is licensed under the GPL, version 2 or later, like WordPress. Your license gives you activation,
        updates and support while it is active; it doesn't limit your rights under the GPL. Pro needs the free plugin and
        the WordPress and PHP versions listed on the plugin's page.
      </p>

      <h2>Free trial</h2>
      <p>
        The 14-day trial of the Creator plan needs no payment card. When it ends, Pro stops unless you buy a license, and
        nothing is charged.
      </p>

      <h2>Renewals and cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Licenses are paid monthly or yearly and renew automatically until you cancel. If the price changes, the new price
        applies from your next renewal after we have told you by email, so you can cancel first.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can cancel at any time from your Freemius account or by emailing us. Pro keeps working until the end of the
        period you paid for, then stops finding sources and checking drafts. The free plugin and every draft you created
        keep working.
      </p>

      <h2>14-day money-back guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        If Pro isn't right for you, email us within 14 days of any payment, including a renewal, and we refund that payment
        in full through Freemius to the way you paid. You don't need to give a reason. The guarantee is in addition to your
        rights as a consumer.
      </p>

      <h2>Your AI and search accounts</h2>
      <p>
        Pro uses your own AI provider account and your own Tavily account, with keys you add to your site. Those providers
        bill you directly, under their own terms, and we don't control their prices, limits or availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Reviewing what you publish</h2>
      <p>
        Generated drafts can contain errors, unsupported claims or out-of-date facts. Pro's claim-to-source check and link
        check help you find problems but can't guarantee a draft is accurate or complete. Neither plugin ever publishes
        automatically: you decide what to publish and are responsible for it.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair use</h2>
      <p>
        Use a license only on the number of sites your plan covers, and don't share, sell or publish license keys. Don't
        use Pro to produce content that breaks the law or the terms of your AI provider. We may suspend a license that is
        used this way, after telling you why.
      </p>

      <h2>Support and updates</h2>
      <p>
        While your license or trial is active you get Pro updates and email support
        at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. We answer as soon as we can, usually within two
        working days.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Pro is provided as it is, to the extent the law allows. Our total liability for any claim about Pro is limited to
        what you paid for it in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does
        not allow to be limited, such as for intent or gross negligence, or your rights as a consumer, including the legal
        guarantee that digital content conforms to the contract.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. Changes apply to new purchases from the date above, and to existing licenses from their
        next renewal after we have told you by email.
      </p>

      <h2>Law and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Portuguese law. If you are a consumer, you keep the protections of the law of the
        country where you live that can't be waived, and you can bring a claim in its courts.
      </p>
      <p>
        If something goes wrong, please email us first. You can also file a complaint
        in the <a href="https://www.livroreclamacoes.pt/">Livro de Reclamações Eletrónico</a> (the Portuguese electronic
        complaints book). Consumers can take a dispute to an alternative dispute resolution body,
        such as <a href="https://www.cniacc.pt/">CNIACC</a>, the Portuguese national consumer arbitration centre;
        the <a href="https://www.consumidor.gov.pt/">Portal do Consumidor</a> lists the others.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
